<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jesus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 4 BCE – c. 30/33 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a> · Also known as Jesus of Nazareth, Jesus Christ</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jesus of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nazareth">Nazareth</a> was a Jewish preacher from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galilee">Galilee</a> whose life and teaching are the basis of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a>. He taught in Galilee and the surrounding regions under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herod-antipas">Herod Antipas</a> and was crucified at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> on the orders of the Roman prefect Pontius Pilate, around 30–33 CE. His followers proclaimed his resurrection and spread the new faith across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a> and beyond.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jesus.jpg" alt="Jesus" width="320" height="622" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown artistUnknown artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Spas_vsederzhitel_sinay_(cropped1).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
